<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB U.S. unit offers $150mln securities.</title>
<headline>AIB U.S. unit offers $150mln securities.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Irish Banks said on Friday that its U.S. unit First Maryland Bancorp is proceeding with an offering of $150 million of trust preferred capital securities with a coupon of one percent over LIBOR at a price of 98.075 pct.</p>
<p>It said the funding will be deductible for taxation proposes and qualify as Tier one capital in the United States.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353-1-6613377I</p>
</text>
